sase-gj[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Diff-scoped lane latency — escalate on estimated runtime, not file [/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]         [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]count[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]`just check`'s scoped test stage is never slower than `just [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]check-full` would have been, the full-suite escalations it does [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]take are attributable to the agent's own diff, and `just [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]selection-health` reports the tail and the flake-free [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]false-negative count instead of hiding both.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]7[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]4[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plans:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]scoped_lane_latency.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/scoped_lane_latency.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-gj[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-gj/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Per-test-file duration table recorded by the full lane[/bold #D7AFFF]        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]timings[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]timings: record per-test-file wall seconds from full-lane runs into the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]host-local store and expose an `estimate_serial_seconds()` the selector [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]can call, with an explicit no-data answer.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Escalate on estimated serial runtime, not on the file-count [/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]ratio[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]budget[dim] · [dim][/dim]after timings[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]budget: add a serial-runtime budget rule so a selection that would take [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]longer than the governed full lane escalates, and keep the file-count [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]ratio only as a fallback when no timing data exists.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]A bounded-parallelism middle gear for large selections[/bold #D7AFFF]        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]gear[dim] · [dim][/dim]after budget[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]gear: let a scoped run that exceeds the serial budget take a small [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]non-blocking lease instead of escalating, falling back to serial rather [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]than ever queueing.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Attribute and narrow the core-identity-changed escalation[/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]identity[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]identity: record which fingerprint input changed, and stop forcing the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]whole suite for environment churn that is byte-identical or already [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]covered by another rule.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Report the scoped lane's tail, not just its median[/bold #D7AFFF]            [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]tail[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]tail: add duration percentiles and a \"slower than the full lane\" counter[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]to `just selection-health` so a latency regression is visible in the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]project's own health metric.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Stop charging known 